### CLI: `aitbc wallet eth-send` — generic Sepolia ETH transfer (CLI-8)

- `aitbc wallet eth-send --to <addr> --amount-eth <dec> --chain-id 11155111` — the first wallet command that sends plain EVM ETH to an explicit recipient (until now every `eth_sendRawTransaction` site had a fixed target: bridge deposit, exchange prepay, float payout). Default is a dry run printing from/to/wei/chain-id/nonce/gas/fee/balance while reading only the wallet's plaintext address — no password, no decrypt, no sign, no broadcast. `--confirm` resolves the wallet password through the standard sources, signs once and broadcasts once; `--wait` polls the receipt. Refusals: every chain id but 11155111 (flag and RPC both checked), zero address, self-send, bad EIP-55 checksum on mixed-case input, zero/negative amount, >18 decimals, amount over `--max-eth` (default 0.1), insufficient balance, `--wait` without `--confirm`.
- Shared helpers factored out of `exchange/prepay.py` into `cli/aitbc_cli/utils/evm_rpc.py` (`rpc_call`, `rpc_try`, `broadcast_raw`, `resolve_rpc_url`, `hex_to_int`) and `commands/wallet/__init__.py` (`_load_signing_key`); prepay keeps its module-level names as delegates so behaviour and the test patch surface are unchanged.
- MCP: `aitbc_wallet_eth_send` regenerated in the safeguarded set — `dry_run`/`confirm` gate plus the CLI's own `--confirm` reaching the tool as `confirm_opt` (a real send needs both true).
- Tests: `cli/tests/test_wallet_eth_send.py`, 23 tests — ephemeral in-process key, fake RPC tables, no network, no real wallet.

