### ETH-3c — bounded log scans in the rehearsal driver

`contracts/scripts/rehearsal/lib.js` + `roundtrip.js`: public RPCs cap
`eth_getLogs` ranges (publicnode `-32701` above 50k blocks) and prune old
logs outright (`4444 pruned history unavailable`), which killed the resumed
run's `BridgeConfirmed` check before any confirm was attempted.
`queryFilterChunked` walks backward in <=40,000-block windows and recursively
halves any window that hits a range cap or straddles the ragged prune
boundary (a single-block pruned window is skipped with a warning; other
errors propagate; 512-window ceiling). Every scan is bounded by
`--from-block`, else the bridge's deployment block (binary-searched via
`eth_getCode`), else `latest-200000`. Confirm scans floor at the deposit
block — a BridgeConfirmed log cannot precede its request. `--lock-tx
<hash>` skips the BridgeInitiated scan entirely by verifying the supplied
receipt carries the log. Dry runs exercise the same bounded scans read-only
and report the adopted request's lockTxHash plus per-signer confirm state.
New hardhat test proves the chunked helper succeeds where one unbounded
query fails under a simulated range cap.

### ETH-3d — lagging-replica-safe read-backs in the rehearsal driver

`contracts/scripts/rehearsal/lib.js` + `roundtrip.js`: `pollRead` re-runs a
read until a predicate holds (20 tries, 1.5 s apart — same bounds as the
Safe-nonce guard) and names the read plus last value if it never holds;
read errors (e.g. a replica not yet knowing a pinned blockTag) are retried.
Every post-transaction read that feeds a decision or assertion now goes
through it with `blockTag` pinned at the last sealed receipt's block:
paused after unpause/pause, supportedTokens after addSupportedToken,
validator flags and the activeValidators listing, requestCounter after
initiateBridge, request status CONFIRMED, bridge and Safe balances after
emergencyWithdraw/transfer, and the final paused+owner check. Skip checks
stay unpolled. Trigger: the continuation run died on a stale `balanceOf`
that answered pre-withdraw state right after a sealed exec. New hardhat
tests: a once-stale `paused()` read recovers; a never-converging read is
reported, not ignored.

