### MSG-2 Phase 1 — votes, moderation and reputation land

- `aitbc/messaging.py`: the v1 codec gains per-kind schemas for eight action kinds — `vote`, `hide`/`unhide`, `pin`/`unpin`, `lock`/`unlock`, `mod_grant`/`mod_revoke`. `target` is a 64-hex tx_hash (required on vote/hide/unhide/pin/unpin, optional on lock/unlock where absent = whole topic); `value` is a strict integer in {-1, 0, +1} (booleans/floats/strings rejected); `grantee` must pass strict canonical-address validation. Unknown kinds remain total-safe — decoding never crashes and other messages still serve. No consensus, state_root or tx-type change: everything is a signed ordinary MESSAGE transaction.
- `messaging_index.py`: the derived index now computes moderation state, standing votes and reputation from sealed rows in canonical (block_height, tx_hash) order. Authority is a fixpoint over ever-moderator-signed grant/revoke rows — never-member spam never enters the scan, and a revoke that would empty the set is ineffective. Hide/pin/lock are independent latest-per-category state; standing votes are an exact SQL ROW_NUMBER partition (no scan bound, no silent truncation); locks apply at their sealed position, never block moderation actions, cover a topic or a reply subtree bounded at LOCK_WALK_LIMIT=512 (fail-open beyond); votes on locked content still count; reputation is Σ clamped per-message score with VOTE_CAP=20, self-votes excluded, display-only.
- RPC: `/rpc/messaging/messages` gains `include_hidden` (hidden/after-lock rows returned flagged, body withheld) and a separate `pinned` list so cursors stay monotone; new `/rpc/messaging/messages/{tx}/votes`, `/rpc/messaging/topics/{slug}/moderation`, `/rpc/messaging/reputation/{address}`; `/rpc/messaging/topics` now reports each topic's founder and moderator set (the pre-activation founder report). Legacy `/rpc/contracts/messaging/*` reputation is repointed to the derived index; the vote/moderate POSTs stay 501 with pointers to the signed-CLI path.
- CLI: `aitbc messaging vote|hide|unhide|pin|unpin|lock|unlock|mod-grant|mod-revoke` submit signed action envelopes through the existing wallet/password flow (`--wait`, `--wait-timeout`, `--rpc-url`, `--fee`, password options preserved); `aitbc messaging reputation|moderators` are read-only. MCP module regenerated — all ten land in the destructive set behind dry_run/confirm.
- Tests: `tests/test_messaging_index_msg2.py` (42 tests) covers codec validation, founder/grant/revoke authority incl. the non-empty-set rule, per-category latest-wins, vote aggregation and topic-mismatch no-ops, lock semantics, cursor monotonicity, reorg removal and reorder/rebuild determinism.

